WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.100
A young neuron grows more branches than it keeps.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.300
Who decides which branch goes?

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:13.783
Pruning removes an axon branch, or a dendrite, from a neuron that survives.

4
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:18.203
Development first builds a rough draft, then carves it.

5
00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:21.143
Think of a sculptor who piles up too much clay.

6
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:27.047
Sympathetic neurons need NGF, a growth factor supplied by their target.

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.970
Now grow them in a dish divided into compartments.

8
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.790
The cell bodies sit in one compartment.

9
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.290
Their branches cross into side compartments.

10
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.970
The fluids stay apart, so each compartment can have NGF, or not.

11
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.943
Remove NGF from one side compartment only.

12
00:00:46.843 --> 00:00:48.203
Which branches degenerate?

13
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.467
Only the branches in that compartment.

14
00:00:57.487 --> 00:01:00.787
Branches of the same neuron next door, still in NGF, stay.

15
00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.867
Now remove NGF from every compartment.

16
00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:09.807
What happens to the neuron?

17
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:19.027
The neuron dies, and its axons go with it.

18
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:22.077
Here is the one idea for this lesson.

19
00:01:22.077 --> 00:01:25.197
Where support is lost decides what is lost.

20
00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:31.567
Lose support at the axons while the cell body keeps it, and the axons degenerate

21
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.567
while the neuron lives.

22
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.650
Lose it everywhere, and the neuron dies.

23
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.320
In the animal, target NGF normally reaches the cell body through signals sent back

24
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.320
along the axons.

25
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.480
So pruning and death follow the same rule.

26
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.680
But they share enzymes, and are wired differently.

27
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.890
Both use caspases, the enzymes of cell death.

28
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.390
So how can one branch use them, and the neuron live?

29
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.840
This rule covers branches lost after support is lost.

30
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.900
Some branches go on a fixed program instead.

31
00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:06.840
Those come later.

32
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.470
So to predict what is lost, first ask where the support was lost.
